359:From the above observation it follows that for every minimum vertex cover $S$ and maximum matching $M$ of a {\Konig} graph $G$, $M$ lies across the edges $(S,V(G) \setminus S)$ and $M$ saturates $S$. Moreover, if there exists a maximum matching $M$ and minimum vertex cover $S$ such that $M$ saturates $S$ and $M$ lies across $(S,V(G)\setminus S)$, then $|M| = |S|$ and hence $G$ must be {\Konig}. So we have the following characterization of {\Konig} graphs.
