+"""Verified Konig-edge-deletion generator for arXiv:1811.04560.
+
+The module implements the parameter-preserving construction in Section 3.
+It inverse-generates a dense graph G with a known k-vertex independent set,
+then forms the paper's graph G' from original vertices V, private vertices P,
+and 2k universal independent vertices C.  Claim 3.3 turns the independent set
+into exactly k private-edge deletions and explicitly supplies an equal-size
+vertex cover and matching in G'-F.
+
+The full graph is encoded without expanding its two complete V/P--C joins:
+the base-edge list plus the displayed construction rules determine every edge.
+Verification expands those rules in memory and checks the cover and matching
+certificate exactly.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
