The first adversary run exposed a real failure: on the simple planted random graph, the standard bitset branch-and-color algorithm recovered the deletion set on every tested instance, so that distribution cannot ship. I’m replacing only the source of the known independent set—not the paper reduction—with a balanced planted 3-CNF conflict graph, which composes an inverse-generated satisfying assignment with the paper’s parameter-preserving construction. This is specifically to make the domain-standard attack confront the CSP structure instead of a statistically visible clique.
