codex
The initial planted-random-graph route fails G6: even after making the source graph exactly regular and hiding the planted set below the basic spectral threshold, randomized minimum-degree greedy recovers a valid independent set on every shipping trial. I’m switching to a Track B family based on the same paper-licensed Section 3 reduction: the source independent-set graph is a succinct affine-permutation constraint graph with a unique cycle certificate. Generic finite-domain propagation must try millions of roots, while the compact route is the cycle’s affine fixed-point invariant. This keeps the König-deletion witness native and exactly checkable, and it is honest about the efficient algorithm that exists.
apply patch
