src/main-file.tex:478:Clearly, $V_1$ and $V_2$ partition $V$. Since $I$ and $P$ are independent, there are no edges in $(P,P)$ and $(I,I)$ and so all edges of $(V_2,V_2)$ are in $(P,I)$. There are exactly $k$ many such edges because every vertex in $P$ is a pendant vertex and $|I|=k$. So $|F|= |(V_2,V_2)| = k$. We claim that $G'[V'\setminus F]$ is a {\Konig} graph. 
