src/main-file.tex:502:Let $F$ be the {\Konig} edge deletion set of size $k$. Let $S'$ be the minimum vertex cover of $G'[E' \setminus F]$ given by Claim \ref{claim:redn_vc_size} such that $C \subseteq S'$ and $P \subseteq V'\setminus S'$. Suppose that there exists an edge $e \in (S',S') \cap F$ or an edge $e \in (S',V'\setminus S') \cap F$ then we can add $e$ back into the graph (by deleting from $F$) and the resulting graph will still remain {\Konig} by Lemma ~\ref{lem:konig_partition}. However, this gives us a {\Konig} edge deletion set of size $k-1$ contradicting Corollary~\ref{cor:konigsize}. 
