+"""Verified Konig-edge-deletion generator for arXiv:1811.04560.
+
+The module implements the parameter-preserving construction in Section 3.
+It inverse-generates a balanced satisfiable 3-CNF, converts its literal
+occurrences into a conflict graph G with a known independent set, then forms
+the paper's graph G' from original vertices V, private vertices P, and 2k
+universal independent vertices C.  Claim 3.3 turns the independent set into
+exactly k private-edge deletions and explicitly supplies an equal-size vertex
+cover and matching in G'-F.
+
+The full graph is encoded without expanding its two complete V/P--C joins:
+the base-edge list plus the displayed construction rules determine every edge.
+Verification expands those rules in memory and checks the cover and matching
+certificate exactly.
+"""
